  "_second_instance": "OPTIONAL (2026-10-01). A second monitored phone runs as a SECOND INSTANCE of this script with its own config file (`eyeguard-phone.py --conf /etc/eyeguard/phone-jada.json`, service eyeguard-phone-jada), written by deploy/jada_phone_install.sh -- do not add these keys to THIS file. Keys that only a second instance sets: device_app (flags `app` label, default \"iPhone\"), reason_prefix (default \"\"; a second device MUST set one so the server never evaluates its events against phone_status id=1 / the Find My cross-check, which are this phone's), heartbeat_rpc (default eg_phone_heartbeat), dark_verdict (default flagged), secondary_instance (true = leave the router config check and sleep relay to the primary). Server side: supabase/jada_phone.sql.",
  "_querylog": "OPTIONAL (all have defaults). AdGuard query-log reader/watcher. querylog_max_lag_seconds = how far behind real time AdGuard's batched log may run before 'log stopped' alerts (default 14400 while size_memory is 1000; tighten to ~900 after size_memory is lowered). querylog_missing_alerts = email when wire queries are absent from the log (default false = log-only until watched on the live router).",
  "querylog_max_lag_seconds": 14400,
  "querylog_missing_alerts": false,
